+H045 retains the complete learned H042 model and adds a paired episode adapter. A maximal consecutive run of the same exact proper sampled-leaf clade is an episode. Reappearance after an absent tree starts a new episode. The same unary representative rule applies, without asserting biological ancestor identity. For a member $i$ with first-sweep state $h_i$ and physical span $w_i$, the foreign context excludes its own tree,
+\begin{equation}
+m_i=\frac{\sum_{j\in E(i)}w_jh_j-w_ih_i}
+           {\sum_{j\in E(i)}w_j-w_i}.
+\end{equation}
+Only episodes containing at least two trees receive an extra residual,
+\begin{equation}
+\Delta_i^{\mathrm{ep}}=
+O_e\!\left[(U_eh_i)\odot(V_em_i)+W_eh_i\right].
+\end{equation}
+The own-state arm substitutes $m_i=h_i$ on the same eligible nodes while computing the same pool. Three bias-free $32\to8$ projections and one $8\to32$ projection add 1,024 weights, for 31,812 per arm. The output projection starts at zero. The second shared tree sweep receives $b+\Delta+\Delta^{\mathrm{ep}}$. PyG sums implement the span-weighted pool, and gradients remain connected across episode members. This is an implemented conditioning comparison, not a claim of a new pooling or message-passing operator. Provenance: E13--E14.
